.SH NAME
anpu-version - Print the ANPU version


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu version [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the ANPU version and build metadata.

.PP
This prints exactly the same line as \fBanpu --version\fR — the two
forms are identical by construction, both rendering
version.Full() from pkg/version.

.PP
The version, commit, and build date are injected at release time by
GoReleaser (see .goreleaser.yaml). Source builds report the version only,
with the commit and date shown as "unknown".


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for version


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


